---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const weakSignals = [
  {
    number: "01",
    title: "The task is vague",
    text:
      "AI knows the general topic but not exactly what action you want it to perform.",
    example: "Help me with inventory.",
  },
  {
    number: "02",
    title: "Important context is missing",
    text:
      "The instruction makes sense to you because you know the situation, but AI does not have that background.",
    example: "Write a reply about the delay.",
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "The output is undefined",
    text:
      "AI has to decide whether you want an email, summary, table, checklist, explanation or something else.",
    example: "Explain our stock problem.",
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "The audience is unclear",
    text:
      "The same information may need very different wording for a customer, manager or frontline employee.",
    example: "Prepare an explanation of the issue.",
  },
  {
    number: "05",
    title: "There are no useful boundaries",
    text:
      "AI may add assumptions, unnecessary detail or recommendations outside the intended scope.",
    example: "Tell me what caused this shortage.",
  },
  {
    number: "06",
    title: "Too many instructions compete",
    text:
      "A prompt can also become weak when it contains unnecessary or conflicting requirements.",
    example: "Be extremely detailed, but answer in two sentences.",
  },
];

const improvementSteps = [
  {
    label: "TASK",
    question: "What exactly should AI do?",
    improvement:
      "Change a broad request into one clear action.",
  },
  {
    label: "CONTEXT",
    question: "What does AI need to know?",
    improvement:
      "Add only the facts that materially affect the answer.",
  },
  {
    label: "AUDIENCE",
    question: "Who will use the result?",
    improvement:
      "Identify the reader when it affects tone, terminology or detail.",
  },
  {
    label: "OUTPUT",
    question: "What should the result look like?",
    improvement:
      "Specify the useful structure, length or format.",
  },
  {
    label: "BOUNDARIES",
    question: "What should AI avoid?",
    improvement:
      "Add constraints where assumptions or unwanted actions could create problems.",
  },
  {
    label: "REVIEW",
    question: "What still needs human checking?",
    improvement:
      "Verify facts, decisions and important conclusions before using the output.",
  },
];

const checklist = [
  "Can I identify one clear task?",
  "Does AI have the facts needed to understand the situation?",
  "Is the intended audience clear when it matters?",
  "Have I defined a useful output format?",
  "Have I removed unnecessary or conflicting instructions?",
  "Have I prevented important unsupported assumptions?",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Improving a Weak Prompt | KRIYANO"
  description="Learn a practical step-by-step method for identifying weak AI prompts and improving them with clearer tasks, context, output requirements and constraints."
>
  <article class="article-page">
    <header class="article-hero">
      <div class="container article-hero-grid">
        <div class="article-heading">
          <a href="/learn/" class="back-link">← LEARN</a>

          <div class="article-meta">
            <span>PROMPTING FUNDAMENTALS</span>
            <span>08</span>
            <span>BEGINNER</span>
          </div>

          <h1>
            Improving a
            <span>Weak Prompt.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="article-intro">
            When AI gives you a weak result, you usually do not need to rewrite
            everything from scratch. Diagnose what is missing, improve the
            instruction that matters, and test again.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="lesson-panel">
          <div class="panel-header">
            <span>LESSON 08</span>
            <span>PROMPTING FUNDAMENTALS</span>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-content">
            <span class="panel-kicker">THE IMPROVEMENT LOOP</span>

            <strong>
              Diagnose → improve → generate → review.
            </strong>

            <p>
              Treat prompting as an iterative process rather than trying to
              create a perfect instruction on the first attempt.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-footer">
            <span>FIND THE GAP → FIX THE GAP</span>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="article-body-section">
      <div class="container article-layout">
        <aside class="article-sidebar">
          <div class="sidebar-box">
            <span class="sidebar-title">IN THIS GUIDE</span>

            <a href="#weak">Why prompts fail</a>
            <a href="#signals">Six signs of a weak prompt</a>
            <a href="#method">A practical improvement method</a>
            <a href="#example">Weak to stronger</a>
            <a href="#iteration">Improve through iteration</a>
            <a href="#checklist">Prompt checklist</a>
            <a href="#takeaway">The practical takeaway</a>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <main class="article-content">
          <section id="weak">
            <div class="section-marker">01 / THE CORE IDEA</div>

            <h2>A weak result does not always mean AI cannot do the task.</h2>

            <p>
              Sometimes the model simply did not receive enough direction. If
              the task, context or expected output is unclear, AI has to fill
              the gaps itself.
            </p>

            <p>
              Before abandoning the task, inspect the prompt. Identify the
              specific information or instruction that would make the expected
              result clearer.
            </p>

            <div class="concept-box">
              <span>DON'T JUST SAY</span>

              <p>
                “Make it better.” Tell AI what is wrong with the current result
                or what specifically needs to change.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="signals">
            <div class="section-marker">02 / DIAGNOSE THE PROMPT</div>

            <h2>Six common signs that your prompt needs improvement.</h2>

            <div class="signals-grid">
              {
                weakSignals.map((item) => (
                  <article class="signal-card">
                    <span>{item.number}</span>

                    <h3>{item.title}</h3>

                    <p>{item.text}</p>

                    <div class="signal-example">
                      <span>EXAMPLE</span>
                      <p>{item.example}</p>
                    </div>
                  </article>
                ))
              }
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="method">
            <div class="section-marker">03 / IMPROVEMENT METHOD</div>

            <h2>Fix the prompt one useful layer at a time.</h2>

            <p>
              Instead of making the prompt longer at random, work through the
              areas that most often affect output quality.
            </p>

            <div class="method-list">
              {
                improvementSteps.map((item, index) => (
                  <div class="method-row">
                    <span class="method-number">
                      {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
                    </span>

                    <div class="method-name">
                      <span>{item.label}</span>
                      <strong>{item.question}</strong>
                    </div>

                    <p>{item.improvement}</p>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </div>

            <div class="decision-box">
              <span>IMPORTANT</span>

              <p>
                You do not have to add all six layers. Fix the parts that are
                actually causing ambiguity.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="example">
            <div class="section-marker">04 / WEAK → STRONGER</div>

            <h2>Watch how a vague workplace prompt becomes more useful.</h2>

            <div class="prompt-stage">
              <div class="stage-header">
                <span>VERSION 01</span>
                <strong>Too vague</strong>
              </div>

              <p class="stage-prompt">
                Write a report about the stock difference.
              </p>

              <div class="stage-problem">
                <span>PROBLEM</span>
                <p>
                  AI does not know the quantities, investigation status,
                  audience, required format or whether the cause is confirmed.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="stage-arrow">↓</div>

            <div class="prompt-stage">
              <div class="stage-header">
                <span>VERSION 02</span>
                <strong>Add context</strong>
              </div>

              <p class="stage-prompt">
                Write a report about an inventory discrepancy. System stock is
                620 units and verified physical stock is 597 units.
              </p>

              <div class="stage-problem">
                <span>BETTER, BUT...</span>
                <p>
                  The task now has facts, but AI still does not know the
                  investigation status or how the report should be structured.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="stage-arrow">↓</div>

            <div class="prompt-stage final-stage">
              <div class="stage-header">
                <span>VERSION 03</span>
                <strong>Clear and controlled</strong>
              </div>

              <p class="stage-prompt">
                Act as an inventory control supervisor. Prepare a concise
                inventory discrepancy report for the inventory manager. System
                stock is 620 units and two verified physical counts show 597
                units, creating a shortage of 23 units. Receiving, outbound and
                adjustment transactions have been reviewed, but the root cause
                has not been confirmed. Use the headings Variance, Checks
                Completed, Findings and Recommended Next Action. Do not invent
                a cause for the discrepancy.
              </p>

              <div class="stage-success">
                <span>WHY IT IS STRONGER</span>

                <div>
                  <p>✓ Clear task</p>
                  <p>✓ Relevant context</p>
                  <p>✓ Defined audience</p>
                  <p>✓ Required structure</p>
                  <p>✓ Important constraint</p>
                  <p>✓ No unsupported conclusion</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="iteration">
            <div class="section-marker">05 / ITERATE</div>

            <h2>You can improve the result without rebuilding the whole prompt.</h2>

            <p>
              If the first response is close but not quite right, give targeted
              follow-up instructions.
            </p>

            <div class="iteration-grid">
              <div>
                <span>TOO LONG?</span>
                <p>
                  “Keep the same information but reduce the summary to 150
                  words.”
                </p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>TOO TECHNICAL?</span>
                <p>
                  “Rewrite this in simple English for a non-technical manager.”
                </p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>WRONG FORMAT?</span>
                <p>
                  “Keep the content but convert the recommendations into a
                  five-step checklist.”
                </p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <span>TOO GENERIC?</span>
                <p>
                  “Make the recommendations specific to the warehouse facts I
                  provided.”
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="iteration-flow">
              <div>
                <span>01</span>
                <strong>Generate</strong>
                <p>Get the first useful draft.</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>02</span>
                <strong>Inspect</strong>
                <p>Identify what is weak.</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>03</span>
                <strong>Adjust</strong>
                <p>Give a specific correction.</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>04</span>
                <strong>Review</strong>
                <p>Check the revised result.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="checklist">
            <div class="section-marker">06 / QUICK CHECK</div>

            <h2>Use this checklist when a prompt is not giving you what you need.</h2>

            <div class="checklist">
              {
                checklist.map((item, index) => (
                  <div class="check-row">
                    <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
                    <p>{item}</p>
                    <strong>✓</strong>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </div>

            <div class="warning-box">
              <span>DON'T CONFUSE PROMPT QUALITY WITH FACTUAL ACCURACY</span>

              <p>
                A well-written prompt can improve relevance and consistency,
                but it cannot guarantee that every AI-generated statement is
                correct. Important facts and decisions still require review.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="takeaway">
            <div class="section-marker">07 / PRACTICAL TAKEAWAY</div>

            <h2>Improve prompts by diagnosing the problem, not by adding random detail.</h2>

            <p>
              When a result is weak, identify what AI misunderstood or lacked.
              Then make the smallest useful improvement and generate again.
            </p>

            <div class="takeaway-flow">
              <div>
                <span>01</span>
                <strong>Diagnose</strong>
                <p>What went wrong?</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>02</span>
                <strong>Improve</strong>
                <p>Fix the missing instruction.</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>03</span>
                <strong>Test</strong>
                <p>Generate another result.</p>
              </div>

              <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>

              <div>
                <span>04</span>
                <strong>Review</strong>
                <p>Keep improving if needed.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tool-callout">
              <div>
                <span class="tool-kicker">PRACTICE WITH KRIYANO</span>

                <h3>Turn a rough instruction into a structured prompt.</h3>

                <p>
                  Use the KRIYANO Prompt Builder to separate the task, context,
                  audience, format, tone and constraints so you can see which
                  parts of your prompt need improvement.
                </p>
              </div>

              <a href="/tools/prompt-builder/" class="button button-primary">
                Open Prompt Builder
              </a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="completion-box">
            <span class="completion-kicker">LEARNING PATH COMPLETE</span>

            <h2>Prompting Fundamentals</h2>

            <p>
              You have covered prompt structure, context, roles, constraints,
              examples and iterative improvement. The next step is applying
              these skills to practical workplace tasks and workflows.
            </p>

            <div class="completion-lessons">
              <span>05 — Anatomy of a Good Prompt</span>
              <span>06 — How to Give AI Better Context</span>
              <span>07 — Using Roles, Constraints & Examples</span>
              <span>08 — Improving a Weak Prompt</span>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="next-lesson">
            <div>
              <span class="next-label">NEXT LEARNING PATH</span>

              <h2>Using AI for Real Work</h2>

              <p>
                Next, learn how to choose suitable tasks for AI, build
                AI-assisted workflows, review output and create reusable
                prompts for recurring work.
              </p>
            </div>

            <a
  href="/learn/using-ai-for-real-work/choosing-tasks-for-ai/"
  class="next-status"
>
  START PATH →
</a>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

